course: dictionary
lesson: 13758
title: Crossing borders: internationally
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «internationally» is long, but you can break it into parts. Inter- means between, national means of a country, and -ly tells you how something happens. So internationally means between or among different countries, or all over the world.
explain: «The band is known internationally.» Think about what this tells you. People in many countries have heard of the band, not just people in one town. The word shows that something crosses borders.
explain: Here is a check you can use. Swap your meaning into the sentence. «The band is known across many countries.» If that still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: Internationally means between or among different countries, or all over the world.
fact: Inter- means between, and national means of a country, so international means between countries.
fact: «Traded internationally» means sold to and bought from other countries.
fact: «The metre is agreed internationally» means countries have all agreed to use the same measure.
fact: Nationally means within one country, but internationally means across many countries.
exercise: «The film is known internationally.» What does internationally mean here? | *Across many countries | Only in one small town | Very quietly | Inside a small house
exercise: Which word in «The metre is agreed internationally.» shows that the agreement crosses borders? | *internationally | metre | the | is
exercise: Ella says internationally is just a long way of saying nationally. What is the difference? | Internationally means at night | They mean exactly the same thing | Nationally means over the sea | *Nationally means within one country, and internationally means across many countries
test: «The café sells its cakes internationally.» Internationally means | Late at night | Only at the café | Very slowly | *In many countries
test: Which sentence shows that something crosses borders? | The shop is open on Sunday. | My bike has a flat tyre. | *The singer is famous internationally. | The room is painted blue.
exam: «The festival attracts visitors internationally.» Which word tells us the visitors come from many countries? | attracts | festival | visitors | *internationally
